The absolute simplest way to build a website without writing code is by using an AI website builder or a drag-and-drop website platform.

Step 1: Pick a Website Builder

Choose a platform depending on your goal:

For single-page sites or landing pages (Fastest & Simplest): Use Carrd. It’s free, minimal, and ideal for quick personal pages or links.
For general business, blogs, or portfolios: Use Wix, GoDaddy, or Squarespace. Their AI assistants generate a ready-made site in minutes based on a short description of what you need.
For online stores: Use Shopify or Wix.

Step 2: Use AI to Draft the Website

1. Sign up for your chosen platform (most offer free trials or free tiers).
2. Choose the option to Generate with AI or select a Template.
3. Enter basic details about your site (e.g., "A personal portfolio for a graphic designer" or "A local bakery page with a menu").
4. The platform will automatically set up your layout, images, and starter text.

Step 3: Customize Content

 Double-click any text box to add your own writing.
Replace placeholder images with your photos.
 Add key pages if needed (e.g., Home, About, Contact).


Step 4: Publish

1. Click Publish.
2. Your site will immediately be live on a free web address (e.g., `yoursite.wixsite.com` or `yoursite.carrd.co`).
3. (Optional) Connect a custom domain name (e.g., `yourname.com`) through the platform's settings if you want a professional Web address.
